   "evidence": "grep `subsemiringClosure` in mathlib/Mathlib/Algebra/Ring/Subsemiring/Basic.lean: `def subsemiringClosure (M : Submonoid R) : Subsemiring R := { AddSubmonoid.closure (M : Set R) with one_mem' := ..., mul_mem' := MulMemClass.mul_mem_add_closure }`; no use of `subsemiringClosure` anywhere in code/TauCeti. PR lines 46-58 reprove the same `mul_mem'` by double `AddSubmonoid.closure_induction`, and lines 64-66 restate `subsemiringClosure_toAddSubmonoid` as `extensionCone.toAddSubmonoid_eq`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/FieldTheory/RealClosure/OrderExtension.lean",
   "fix": "Make `weightedSquares f : Submonoid L` (carrier `{x | \u2203 a, 0 \u2264 a \u2227 \u2203 y, x = f a * y ^ 2}`, `one_mem' := \u27e81, zero_le_one, 1, by simp\u27e9`, `mul_mem'` := the existing `weightedSquares_mul` body) and set `def extensionCone (f) : Subsemiring L := (weightedSquares f).subsemiringClosure`. Then `extensionCone.toAddSubmonoid_eq` is `Submonoid.subsemiringClosure_toAddSubmonoid` (line 434), `extensionCone.induction` is `AddSubmonoid.closure_induction` through `Submonoid.subsemiringClosure_mem` (line 430), and `extensionCone.le_iff` follows from `Submonoid.subsemiringClosure_eq_closure` (line 447) with `Subsemiring.closure_le`.",
   "issue": "`extensionCone f` is defined as `AddSubmonoid.closure (weightedSquares f)` with a hand-rolled nested `closure_induction` proof of `mul_mem'` and an inline `one_mem'`. Mathlib's `Submonoid.subsemiringClosure` (Mathlib/Algebra/Ring/Subsemiring/Basic.lean:421) does this assembly, with `mul_mem' := MulMemClass.mul_mem_add_closure` (Mathlib/Algebra/Ring/Submonoid/Basic.lean:33). The private `weightedSquares_mul` and the `one_mem'` term are precisely the data of a `Submonoid`.",
   "line": 46
  }
 ],
